   "title": "Vector retrieval with embeddings",
   "content": {
    "markdown": "Vector retrieval converts queries and passages into numerical embeddings using an encoder model, then returns passages with embeddings closest to the query's. This allows matching passages with similar meanings even without shared words, addressing vocabulary mismatch. However, embeddings are less effective for exact codes and identifiers, as similar codes may appear nearly identical to the encoder, and rare product names might be fragmented. In tests, vector retrieval alone missed 31 out of 50 queries primarily consisting of error codes. Additionally, embeddings require recomputation (approximately 6 hours for this collection) whenever the encoder model changes."
